.TH VISIONFS 4
.SH NAME
visionfs \- recognition as files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B visionfs
[
.B -m
.I mountpoint
] [
.B load
.I name dir
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Visionfs
serves recognition models as files, mounted by default at
.BR /mnt/vision :
a program, a person at the shell, or an agent writes a picture and
reads back what is in it, one record a line.
Which machine does the looking is which server is mounted there: this
one, or another's, over 9P.
.PP
A model is a directory made by
.BR tools/vision/onnx2vis.py :
.BR graph ,
.BR weights ,
.BR classes ,
.B info
and
.BR sha256 .
Its weights are refused unless their SHA-256 is the one recorded, and
its graph is checked, every operation's numbers and every tensor's
shape, before anything runs.
It is run by
.B /dis/lib/visnet.dis
on
.BR $Tensor ,
the processor's arithmetic (see
.IR tensor (2)).
.PP
To mount it from another Dis VM
.RI ( vm (1)),
post its mount:
.B post vision /mnt/vision
.RI ( post (1)).
.I Load
loads a model as the server starts, as
.B ctl
does.
.SS Files
.TF models/\fIname\fP/classes
.TP
.B ctl
Written:
.BI load " name dir"
loads the model in
.I dir
as
.IR name ;
.BI unload " name"
lets it go, refused while a session uses it.
.BI engine " dir"
attaches an engine tree mounted at
.IR dir :
the Jetson's GPU and DLAs, served by
.B trtsrv
.RB ( tools/trtsrv )
on its host command's pipe and mounted by whoever builds the name space;
.B "engine none"
lets it go, refused while a session is on one of its places.
Read: the engine
.RB ( "engine cpu" ,
and
.BI "engine trt " dir
with one), where a session may run
.RB ( "places cpu" ,
or
.B "places cpu gpu dla0 dla1"
with an engine tree), and each model,
.BI model " name dir" .
.TP
.BI models/ name /info
.B kind=detect decode=yolox input=416x416 classes=80 order=bgr fill=114 places=cpu sha256=...
.br
.B places
lists
.B cpu
and, with an engine tree, the places the model's directory has engines
for
.RB ( engines/sha256 ,
from
.BR tools/trtsrv/mkengines.sh ).
.TP
.BI models/ name /classes
One class name a line, in index order.
.TP
.B clone
Read: a new session's number,
.IR N .
The session lasts while any of its files is open, this one included.
.TP
.IB N /ctl
A setting a line, written as read:
.BI src " feed"
(a directory of the
.IR vid9p (1)
schema:
.BR fmt ,
.BR frame ,
.BR status )
or
.BR "src none" ,
.BI rate " fps"
(frames a second at most; 0, as many as it can),
.BI model " name" \fR,
.BI place " p"
(where its network runs:
.B cpu
at first, or one of the model's places; on another, its engine is put into
the engine tree the first time a session asks for it, and the heads it
gives are decoded here as on the processor),
.BI thresh " r"
(0 to 1; 0.30 at first),
.BI iou " r"
(boxes of one class overlapping by this or more are kept once; 0.45),
.BI classes " name ..."
or
.BR "classes all" .
Every line of a write is checked before any is done, and a refusal says
why.
A new session has the first model loaded.
.TP
.IB N /image
A picture, in any format
.IR imgload (2)
reads or a binary PPM, in as many writes as it takes from its start; it
is looked at when the file is closed.
.TP
.IB N /detections
Following a feed, each read is one frame's records, every line beginning
.BI frame= n
.BI pts= ms\fR,
a frame with nothing in it that alone; a read waits for the next frame,
a reader that opens it late starts at the next frame, one that has fallen
behind what is kept is first told
.BI gap " n=k" \fR,
and the end of the feed is the end of the file.
The detector takes the newest frame each time it is ready for one and
never holds the feed back; a clip that has ended is looked at whole.
Otherwise, what was found in the last picture, best first, one record a line:
.IP
.EX
class=dog score=0.86 x0=133 y0=207 x1=326 y1=543
.EE
.IP
in the picture's pixels,
.B x0 y0
inside the box and
.B x1 y1
just past it.
A read waits while the picture is looked at.
Nothing found is nothing read.
.TP
.IB N /layer/vision. N
The same records, as a layer to bind into a video's stack.
.TP
.IB N /status
.BI state= state
.RB ( idle ,
.BR running ,
.BR ready ,
.BR error )
and
.BI model= name\fR,
with
.BI reason= ...
when something is wrong.
.TP
.IB N /stats
Following a feed:
.BI in= n
frames,
.BI inferred= n
looked at,
.BI skipped= n
not,
.BI fps_infer= r\fR,
.B ms_p50=
and
.B ms_p95=
a frame,
.BI readers= n\fR.
Otherwise
.BI images= n
looked at,
.BI found= n
in the last,
.BI ms= n
it took.
.PD
.PP
Each picture is looked at in a process of its own, so one session's
never holds up another's, nor the server.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
; visionfs load nano /lib/vision/yolox-nano
; {
	id=`{read}
	cat photo.jpg > /mnt/vision/$id/image
	cat /mnt/vision/$id/detections
} < /mnt/vision/clone
class=dog score=0.86 x0=133 y0=207 x1=326 y1=543
class=bicycle score=0.80 x0=54 y0=137 x1=572 y1=423
.EE
.PP
On a machine with no model of its own, another's:
.EX
; mount tcp!orin!vision /mnt/vision
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/visionfs.b
.br
.B /appl/lib/visnet.b
.br
.B /tools/vision/onnx2vis.py
.SH EXAMPLES
Recognition on the Jetson's first DLA:
.IP
.EX
mount -A {os trtsrv >[1=0]} /mnt/trt
visionfs load yolox /lib/vision/yolox-nano
echo engine /mnt/trt > /mnt/vision/ctl
{
	id=`{read}
	echo place dla0 > /mnt/vision/$id/ctl
	cat dog.jpg > /mnt/vision/$id/image
	cat /mnt/vision/$id/detections
} < /mnt/vision/clone
.EE
.PP
.B >[1=0]
joins the host command's output to the channel
.B mount
gives it on its input.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR vision (1),
.IR tensor (2)
.SH BUGS
Only detectors of the YOLOX family are converted.
On an engine tree a picture's tensors cross 9P (about 1.6 MB a picture in
FP16), which costs more than the GPU's inference.
A feed's frame numbers are its own only where its
.B status
counts them
.RB ( frames= ,
as
.IR vid9p (1)'s
does); elsewhere they are counted from the start of following.
